# The finned example rocket solved by the 3D engine (BOWSHOCK_ENGINE=3d, Euler today): the fin sector at zero incidence and the half domain at 6 degrees, in the 3D scene
# tiled to the whole rocket, wall Cp on the walls and a meridian Mach sheet through a fin plane. A real solve (a few minutes on the GPU: the headless driver waits for it),
# through the queue:
#   tools/gpuq/gpuq submit --host local --name finned-3d -- env BOWSHOCK_ENGINE=3d ICED_TEST_BACKEND=wgpu \
#     cargo run --release -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/finned-3d.drive out/finned-3d
viewport 1500x1100
click "Analyze"
click "CFD table"
click "Flow field"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot sector-default-dark.png

# the sheets by what they show: the Mach sheet through a fin plane, the sectors tiled to the whole rocket, the walls of the whole rocket coloured by Cp
click "Fin plane"
click "Tile"
click "Whole rocket"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot sector-tiled-fin-plane-dark.png

# the half domain at 6 degrees (the angle stepper: 0, 2, 6)
click "▶"
click "▶"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot half-6deg-tiled-fin-plane-dark.png
